      "html": "<p>Africa: southern Cameroon waters, Ntem and Kyé. Type locality: Mami River, a tributary of Kyé River, Equatorial Guinea.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1306",
      "html": "<p>The genus Microsynodontis has an interrupted lateral line. The caudal fin is usually rounded or truncate, sometimes with a slight indent. There is a long adipose fin with no fin ray. Three pairs of barbels, with the mandibular barbels branched. Etymology: from the Greek mikros, meaning small, and synodontis, in reference to the small size of members of this genus. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
